# Project-Internal Patterns

This rule applies to engineers working **on** ShipAPI itself — the framework monorepo. For consumer-app patterns, see `packages/core/templates/default/.cursor/rules/`.

## Monorepo layout

ShipAPI is an npm-workspaces monorepo:

```
ship-api/
├── packages/
│   ├── core/                       # @sixthsummit/ship-api — the framework
│   │   ├── src/                    # framework source
│   │   ├── cli/                    # ship-api CLI (create / dev / g / migrate-orm / add)
│   │   ├── templates/default/      # v4 reference template (consumed by `ship-api create`)
│   │   ├── lib/                    # build output (.gitignored)
│   │   └── vitest.config.ts        # 80/70 coverage gate
│   ├── claude-plugin/              # @sixthsummit/ship-api-claude-plugin
│   │   ├── agents/                 # ship-architect / ship-codegen / ship-reviewer
│   │   ├── skills/                 # auto-synced summaries of .cursor/rules/
│   │   ├── commands/               # /ship:* slash commands
│   │   └── hooks/                  # PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop
│   └── mcp-server/                 # @sixthsummit/ship-api-mcp-server
├── modules/                        # built-in feature modules
│   ├── accounts/                   # canonical CRUD reference
│   ├── oauth/                      # multi-step flow + provider adapters
│   └── outbox/                     # transactional outbox + drainer
├── libraries/                      # pluggable shared libraries
│   ├── ai/                         # LLMProvider + agent loop + RAG
│   ├── chunking/                   # text chunking
│   ├── email/                      # email helpers
│   └── weaviate/                   # vector store
├── apps/
│   └── docs/                       # Astro + Starlight docs site
├── docs/                           # canonical markdown (V4_LAUNCH, V4_STATUS, MIGRATION_V3_TO_V4, v4/*)
├── scripts/                        # sync-skills / check-skills-sync / build-core / copy-docs / edge-smoke
└── .cursor/rules/                  # canonical project conventions (this directory)
```

## Where things live (framework — `packages/core/src/`)

### `app/` — primitives

- `app/auth/` — `AuthProvider` interface + `FirebaseAuthProvider` adapter
- `app/auth/jwt/` — `JwtSigner` (ES256), `AuthFlow`, `RefreshTokenStore`
- `app/db/` — `client` (drizzle pool), `baseFields` (audit-column mixin), `transaction`, `QueryOptions` (neutral operator DSL)
- `app/schema/` — **removed**; identity/RBAC tables (accounts / roles / permissions / refresh_tokens) now live in `modules/accounts`, core ships no concrete tables
- `app/services/DrizzleEntityService.ts` — generic CRUD/list/search base
- `app/services/jobs/` — `defineJob`, `JobRegistry`, `JobsManager`
- `app/services/cron/` — `defineCron`
- `app/registry/routes.ts` — runtime route registry (read by MCP tools, agents, `/dev/routes`)
- `app/lifecycle/Bootstrapper.ts` — priority + dependsOn ordering
- `app/health/HealthCheck.ts` — `HealthCheckRegistry`
- `app/services/cache/`, `app/services/storage/` — Cache + Disk/S3/GCS adapters

### `http/` — HTTP layer

- `http/app/createApp.ts` — `Hono<AppEnv>` factory with route-method interception that captures `RouteEntry` from middleware tags into the registry
- `http/app/errors.ts` — `registerErrorHandlers(app)` for the AppError taxonomy
- `http/middleware/` — `requireAuth`, `requirePermission`, `apiKey`, `rateLimit`, `idempotency`, `csrf`, `httpLogger`
- `http/utils/validate.ts` — `validate("json"|"query"|"param", schema)` zValidator wrapper
- `http/streaming/` — `streamSSE`, `streamLLM` (SSE bridge for LLM provider streams)
- `http/ws/` — `@hono/node-ws` adapter + subprotocol-header authentication

### `observability/`

- `logger.ts` — pino, ND-JSON in prod, pino-pretty in dev, redaction list
- `otel.ts` — `@opentelemetry/sdk-node` + auto-instrumentations (http / undici / pg / ioredis / pino)
- `metrics.ts` — Prometheus exporter on a separate port
- `tracing.ts` — `withSpan` helper

### `client.ts` — typed-client subpath

Re-exports `hc` from `hono/client` and exposes `ShipApiClient` type. Mapped to `@sixthsummit/ship-api/client` via `package.json#exports`.

## Module pattern (canonical 7-file shape)

Built-in modules under `modules/<name>/` (framework monorepo) and consumer modules at `<project>/modules/<name>/` (scaffolded apps) follow the same shape:

```
<name>/
├── schema.ts                       # Drizzle pgTable + relations + types
├── permissions.ts                  # module:resource:action slug constants
├── validation/schemas.ts           # Zod schemas (.strict() on objects)
├── services/<NameSingular>Service.ts   # extends DrizzleEntityService<typeof table>
├── routes.ts                       # buildXxxApp(deps) → mounts at root; defineXxxRoutes(app, deps) escape hatch
├── index.ts                        # barrel
└── module.json                     # metadata
```

Each module exposes a `buildXxxApp(deps)` that returns its **own bounded sub-app** built on `createModuleApp("xxx")` (a CORS-less `createApp` sibling that tags every route with its module name). The consumer mounts each sub-app onto the root with `root.route("/", buildXxxApp(deps))`. Modules keep their **absolute** paths (`/accounts`, `/accounts/:id`), so mounting at `/` leaves the client shape (`api.accounts.$get`) and the route-registry paths unchanged — no codegen. Mounting each module as its own sub-app (rather than chaining every module's routes onto one app) keeps each module's TypeScript route-type instantiation bounded, so the typed client scales to many modules without `tsc` overflowing its instantiation budget.

```ts
export function buildAccountsApp(deps: { service: AccountService; provider: AuthProvider }) {
  return defineAccountsRoutes(createModuleApp("accounts"), deps);
}

export function defineAccountsRoutes<S extends Schema>(
  app: Hono<AppEnv, S>,
  deps: { service: AccountService; provider: AuthProvider },
) {
  return app
    .get("/accounts", requireAuth({ provider }), requirePermission("accounts:read"), handler)
    .post("/accounts", requireAuth({ provider }), requirePermission("accounts:create"),
                       validate("json", createAccountSchema), handler);
}
```

`defineXxxRoutes(app, deps)` is **kept** (back-compat / advanced composition — deliberately registering a module's routes onto an existing already-typed app) but it is a documented **foot-gun**: threading one shared `app` through several modules' `defineXxxRoutes` calls accumulates one giant Hono route-type and detonates `tsc` (TS2589 / "instantiation excessively deep") once you have enough modules, collapsing the `hc()` client to `never`. Prefer `buildXxxApp` + `root.route("/", ...)`. When you do use the raw form, it must stay **generic over Hono's schema param `S`** — a non-generic `app: Hono<AppEnv>` (or `<T extends Hono<AppEnv>>`) widens an already-chained app, erasing previously wired modules' routes from the client type. It **returns the chained app** so RPC types survive; mutating `(app) => void` registers routes at runtime but loses the type chain.

Read `modules/accounts/` (CRUD), `modules/oauth/` (multi-step flow + provider adapters + state signing), and `modules/outbox/` (transactional outbox + drainer) as canonical references before adding a non-trivial module.

## Plumbing across modules

### Composing schemas

Consumers compose module schema fragments via the `createApp<TSchema>({ schema })` generic:

```ts
import { createApp } from "@sixthsummit/ship-api";
import { accountsSchema } from "./modules/accounts";
import { posts } from "./modules/posts/schema";

const schema = { ...accountsSchema, posts };
const app = createApp({ schema });
// app.db is DrizzleDb<typeof schema> — fully typed, no augmentation needed
```

This **replaces** the abandoned SchemaRegistry + module-augmentation pattern.

### Composing routes (mount-at-root sub-apps)

Cross-cutting concerns live on the **root only** — `registerErrorHandlers`, `httpLogger`, and CORS. Modules must not set their own `onError` or `use("*")` on a sub-app: a sub-app `onError` shadows the uniform AppError shape, and `httpLogger`'s RequestContext must wrap every sub-app from the root. Each module mounts as its own sub-app:

```ts
import { createApp, registerErrorHandlers, httpLogger } from "@sixthsummit/ship-api";

const root = createApp({ cors });
registerErrorHandlers(root);          // root owns cross-cutting concerns
root.use("*", httpLogger());

const app = root
  .route("/", buildAccountsApp({ service: accountService, provider }))
  .route("/", buildPostsApp({ service: postService, provider }));

export type ShipApiClient = typeof app;   // api.accounts.$get — flat shape, unchanged
```

The chain of `root.route("/", buildXxxApp(...))` mounts is the source of truth for the typed client. Order doesn't matter for behavior (Hono routes match on method+path); each `.route("/", subApp)` return type accumulates the mounted sub-app's routes, so the final capture carries every module. Mounting bounded sub-apps (instead of threading one app through every `defineXxxRoutes`) is what keeps `tsc`'s route-type instantiation bounded so the client scales.

For an `hc()` client narrowed to success-status responses, the `@sixthsummit/ship-api/client` subpath also exports `ShipApiSuccessClient<App>` (drops the 4xx/5xx response shapes) for apps that handle errors centrally via `registerErrorHandlers`.

## Bootstrapping

`Bootstrapper` interface gains `priority: number` (lower runs first) + optional `dependsOn: string[]` (validated at boot). Built-in priorities:

| Priority | Bootstrapper | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | InitObservability | OTel SDK shutdown registration |
| 10 | InitFirebaseApp | Firebase Admin SDK init |
| 20 | InitDatabase | Drizzle pool + `db:migrate` |
| 30 | InitRedis | Redis connection + readiness |
| 40 | InitMetricsServer | Prometheus port |
| 50 | InitModules | Route registration |
| 60 | InitJobs | Needs Redis + Modules |
| 65 | InitCron | Needs Jobs |
| 85 | InitDevRoutes | `/dev/routes` HTML view; gated by `WORKER_MODE=local` |
| 90 | InitCustomRoutes | Downstream override hook |
| 100 | InitCustomData | Last; seeds + custom init |

Misordered configs throw at startup, not at first request.

Health routes are not a bootstrapper: `createApp()` mounts unauthenticated `/livez` + `/readyz` by default (`health: false` opts out) and `createDb()` registers a `db.primary` readiness check (`healthCheck: false` opts out). Never add `/healthz` — Cloud Run's front end intercepts it.

## Skills-sync invariant

The plugin's skills (`packages/claude-plugin/skills/*/SKILL.md`) are human-authored summaries of `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. The drift state lives at `scripts/skills-sync-state.json` (committed).

- After editing any rule, run `npm run sync:skills` to recompute hashes.
- Review the corresponding SKILL.md files — if your edit changed the *meaning* (not just wording), update the summary too.
- Commit the rule change + state-file update + any SKILL.md updates together. CI's `npm run check:skills` step will fail otherwise.

The five SKILL.md files map to rule themes (not 1:1 to files):
- `ship-api-conventions/SKILL.md` ← api.mdc + project-patterns.mdc
- `ship-module-pattern/SKILL.md` ← project-patterns.mdc + api.mdc (module shape)
- `ship-drizzle-migrations/SKILL.md` ← api.mdc (migration section)
- `ship-bullmq-jobs/SKILL.md` ← project-patterns.mdc (jobs / cron)
- `ship-otel-debugging/SKILL.md` ← (no rule directly; references observability/otel.ts and logger.ts)

## Public API contract

`packages/core/src/index.ts` is the **stable v4 public API barrel**. Deep-path imports outside the barrel are marked `@internal` in JSDoc and **not** semver-stable.

Stable exports (per `docs/V4_LAUNCH.md` §H):
- `createApp`, `defineSchema`, `defineEnv`, `defineModule`, `defineTool`, `defineHealthCheck`, `defineCron`, `defineJob`
- All AppError subclasses
- `requireAuth`, `requirePermission`, `rateLimit`, `idempotency`, `parseUpload`, `parseWebhook`, `streamSSE`, `streamLLM`
- `DrizzleEntityService`, `Cache`, `JobQueue`, `RedisProvider`, `StorageService` (+ `S3StorageAdapter`, `DiskStorageAdapter`, `GCSStorageAdapter`)
- `withTransaction`, `buildQueryOptions`, types for `QueryOptions`
- `Logger`, `withSpan`, `AppEnv`

The `@sixthsummit/ship-api/client` subpath exports `hc` + `ShipApiClient` type — runtime cost paid only by consumers that import it.

## Runtime route registry

`app/registry/routes.ts` captures per-route metadata from middleware tags:

```ts
interface RouteEntry {
  method: 'GET' | 'POST' | 'PUT' | 'PATCH' | 'DELETE' | 'OPTIONS' | 'HEAD' | 'WS';
  path: string;
  module?: string;
  auth: { required: boolean; provider?: string };
  permissions: string[];
  rateLimit?: { windowMs: number; max: number };
  idempotent?: boolean;
  schemas: { json?: ZodSchema; query?: ZodSchema; param?: ZodSchema; header?: ZodSchema };
  description?: string;
  tags?: string[];
  deprecated?: boolean;
}
```

Population is automatic — `validate(target, schema)`, `requireAuth({...})`, `requirePermission(...)`, `rateLimit({...})`, `idempotency({...})` all tag their returned middleware. `createApp` intercepts route methods, walks middleware tags, and pushes a `RouteEntry`.

Consumed by:
- MCP tools: `list_routes`, `describe_route`, `find_route_collisions`, `execute_route`
- `/dev/routes` HTML debug endpoint
- `ship-reviewer` plugin agent — flags missing schema / auth on mutating routes
- `ship-api g doctor` CLI

## Things framework agents commonly get wrong

- **Don't `console.log` in framework or module code.** Use `logger`. `console.*` writes lose request-id + trace context.
- **Don't read `process.env` directly** outside `defineEnv` / `otel.ts` / `metrics.ts`. Module + handler code routes through the validated `env` object.
- **Don't hand-write SQL migrations.** Use `drizzle-kit generate`. The plugin's `PreToolUse` hook (`block-migration-edit.sh`) blocks edits to `src/db/migrations/*.sql`.
- **Don't import from `lib/`** — those are build artifacts.
- **Don't use `c.req.json()` / `c.req.query()` / `c.req.param()`** directly. Use `validate(...)` + `c.req.valid(...)`. ESLint's `no-restricted-syntax` rule fires on raw use.
- **Don't skip `requireAuth({ provider })` / `requirePermission(slug)`** on protected routes — authorization runs at the route, not the service.
- **Don't shape error responses inside handlers** — throw from the AppError taxonomy. `registerErrorHandlers(app)` shapes the JSON uniformly.
- **Don't enqueue BullMQ jobs inside a transaction** — risks queue-before-commit. Use `OutboxEventEmitter.emit({...}, { tx })`; the drainer enqueues post-commit.
- **Don't thread one shared `app` through several `defineXxxRoutes` calls.** That accumulates one giant route-type and detonates `tsc` (TS2589). Build each module as its own sub-app with `buildXxxApp(deps)` (on `createModuleApp("xxx")`) and mount it via `root.route("/", buildXxxApp(deps))`. If you do reach for the raw `defineXxxRoutes(app, ...)` escape hatch, keep it schema-generic and **return** the chained `app` (never `(app) => void`) so RPC types survive on `hc()` consumers.
- **Don't import test fixtures via source paths (`../../app/...`) when modules import via `@sixthsummit/ship-api/...`** — class identities differ between source and built lib, breaking `instanceof AppError` checks.
- **Don't add `experimentalDecorators: true` anywhere.** v4 uses middleware, not decorators. Decorator metadata was a v3 carry-over and is gone.

## Configuration

- Node ≥22 (engines field).
- TypeScript 5.9, ESLint 10, Vitest 3.x, Prettier 3.x.
- The framework's tsconfig targets ES2022 + NodeNext; consumer template inherits.
- ESLint enforces `no-restricted-syntax` (raw `c.req.json/query/param`), `no-restricted-globals: ['process']` (forces `defineEnv`), `unused-imports/no-unused-imports`.

## CLI

`packages/core/cli/`:
- `commands/create.js` — `ship-api create my-app` (uses `templates/default/`)
- `commands/dev.js` — `ship-api dev` (Docker Compose deps + `tsx watch` + `/livez` polling)
- `commands/generate.js` — `ship-api g {module|resource|service|schema|middleware|job|doctor}`
- `commands/migrate-orm.js` — TypeORM → Drizzle codemod (one-time aid for v3 holdouts)
- `commands/add.js` — `ship-api add <module>` / `add -l <library>`
- `commands/update.js` — `ship-api update`

## Verification

Before declaring framework work done:

1. `npm run type-check` — passes.
2. `npm run lint` — passes.
3. `npm test -w @sixthsummit/ship-api` — passes.
4. `npx vitest run modules/<name>/` — module-specific tests pass.
5. `npm run check:skills` — `.cursor/rules/` ↔ skills hash state in sync.
6. `npm run build -w @sixthsummit/ship-api` — the framework builds cleanly.
7. `npx audit-ci --config .audit-ci.json` — no high/critical findings.
8. `npm run docs:build` — apps/docs builds cleanly.
9. If you touched `http/`: the edge-smoke CI step (`scripts/edge-smoke/`) verifies the bundle still compiles for Cloudflare Workers.
